<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/harness/server/retained',
        '/harness/server/closures',
        '/harness/gate/in-a-fresh-process',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/harness/tests/server.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('retainedPerRun() comes back tagged, with its rep count and its growth'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Find what each run of a lookup keeps">
        <p>The body runs <code>reps</code> times, 1000 by default, and <code>perRep</code> is
            the mean, by engine type, of what each run leaves reachable after a full
            collection. What a run builds and drops is not counted.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { retainedPerRun } from '@abide/harness/server'

            const cache = new Map<string, URL>()
            const answer = retainedPerRun(() => {
                const link = \`https://crm.test/invoices/\${cache.size}\`
                cache.set(link, new URL(link))
            }, 400)
            answer.tagged // 'batch mean'
            answer.perRep // what each run left in the cache, by type
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Check a cache stops growing across the batch">
        <p>The batch is split in two, and <code>growth</code> is the second half's mean minus
            the first's. A type left out of it was kept at the same rate in both halves.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            const answer = retainedPerRun(() => lookup('acme'))
            answer.growth // {} when every run keeps the same
        `} />
        <p>Gate an exact count on <code>retained</code>. A mean is not a count to compare
            with <code>toBe</code>.</p>
    </Section>
</Doc>
